# streams1 — XADD
#
# Learn: a stream is an append-only log of entries, each a small set of
# field/value pairs with an ID "<milliseconds>-<sequence>". IDs must only
# grow. Pass * and the server picks the next ID from its clock, which is
# what you want almost always.
#
# Task: append a signup event (type = signup, user = 42) to the stream
# events, which already has entries. The command below is rejected.
#

XADD events 1 type signup user 42
